, 28 free. Total: 178 active head, 3 active lots, 2 active pens, capacity 230, 52 free.\nProcurement traceability: Prairie Creek Cattle Co. PO-5817 line 2 received Jan 8, 2025, 96 Angus head into Pen 4: L-241 64 head at $1,400/head, allocated purchase cost $89,600; L-242 32 head at $1,400/head, allocated cost $44,800. Mesa Range Livestock PO-5831 line 1 received Mar 1, 2025, 82 Hereford steers into Pen 7 as L-243, $1,460/head, allocated cost $119,720. A mock source PO-5842 line 1 has no receiving quantity and is rejected, not imported. Lots: L-241 Angus steers, received Jan 8, 782 lb average, latest Apr 16 987 lb, target 1,350 lb, 99 days on feed as of Apr 17, measured ADG 2.07 lb/day, FCR 8.69, cost of gain $1.09/lb, projected ship Oct 9, 2025. L-242 Angus heifers, received Jan 8 at 748 lb, Apr 16 931 lb, 99 days on feed, ADG 1.85, FCR 9.12, cost of gain $1.18/lb. L-243 Hereford steers, received Mar 1 at 815 lb, Apr 15 903 lb, 47 days on feed, ADG 1.87, FCR 8.76, cost of gain $1.14/lb. Aggregate weighted average ADG 1.94 lb/day and weighted average cost of gain $1.13/lb. Total feed cost across active lots $29,425.36.\nSaved ration Finisher 18 is intended for 850–1,350 lb cattle: steam-flaked corn 70%, alfalfa hay 20%, cottonseed meal 7%, mineral premix 3%; crude protein 13.2%, TDN 77.4%, net energy 0.82 Mcal/lb; normalized calculated cost $0.1254/lb. Current ingredient costs for its normalized calculation are $0.11/lb corn, $0.09/lb hay, $0.25/lb cottonseed meal, and $0.43/lb mineral premix. Inventory for Apr 1–17: corn opening 50,000 lb, received 5,000, consumed 38,127.6, closing 16,872.4; hay 20,000 + 1,200 − 10,893.6 = 10,306.4 lb; cottonseed meal 8,000 + 0 − 3,812.8 = 4,187.2 lb; mineral premix 2,000 + 300 − 1,634.0 = 666.0 lb. The configured wastage ratio for estimates is 4%; it is not a stock movement. Projection daily demand including wastage: corn 2,333 lb, hay 666 lb, cottonseed meal 233 lb, mineral premix 100 lb. Use horizons of 1, 7, 30, 90, 180, and 365 days.\nPlans: Apr 15 Pen 4 at 18 lb/head/day × 96 head = 1,728 lb, Completed; Apr 16 Pen 7 at 18 × 82 = 1,476 lb, Completed; Apr 17 Pen 4 at 18 × 96 = 1,728 lb, Completed; Apr 18 Pen 7 at 18 × 82 = 1,476 lb, Planned; Apr 19 Pen 4 at 18.5 × 96 = 1,776 lb, Planned. Apr 17 plan lot split: L-241 1,152 lb, L-242 576 lb. Accepted Apr 17 activity returned actual 1,776 lb, +48 lb variance from its plan, Completed; returned inventory consumption corn 1,243.2 lb, hay 355.2 lb, cottonseed meal 124.3 lb, mineral premix 53.3 lb; feed cost $222.71; energy 1,456.3 Mcal; lot allocations L-241 1,184 lb, L-242 592 lb; no web-side stock decrement formula. Lot costs and lot-level performance figures are returned operational values, not recomputed by the UI. Dashboard daily estimated energy use is 2,667 Mcal for the current planned yard feeding.\nOne shared dated event list for histories, activity rows, inventory movements, and sync outcomes (all times America/Denver): Jan 8 07:45, Luis Ortega, received 64 Angus head from PO-5817 line 2 into Pen 4 as L-241, success; Jan 8 08:10, Luis Ortega, received 32 Angus head from PO-5817 line 2 into Pen 4 as L-242, success; Jan 8 08:20, Luis Ortega, weighed L-241 at 782 lb average in Pen 4, accepted; Jan 8 08:35, Luis Ortega, weighed L-242 at 748 lb average in Pen 4, accepted; Feb 19 07:00, Luis Ortega, weighed L-241 at 870 lb average in Pen 4, accepted; Mar 1 09:00, Luis Ortega, received 82 Hereford steers from PO-5831 line 1 into Pen 7 as L-243 at 815 lb average, success; Mar 19 07:00, Luis Ortega, weighed L-241 at 932 lb average in Pen 4, accepted; Apr 1 08:15, Mara Chen, received 5,000 lb corn, 1,200 lb hay, and 300 lb mineral premix into yard inventory, success; Apr 15 08:00, Luis Ortega, completed Pen 4 feeding plan at 1,728 lb, L-241/L-242 allocation proportional to 64:32, accepted; Apr 15 07:00, Luis Ortega, weighed L-243 at 903 lb average in Pen 7, accepted; Apr 16 07:10, Luis Ortega, weighed L-241 at 987 lb average in Pen 4, accepted; A